{"card":{"card_id":"ma-c-a2b84a8a686dbd0c8567","statement":"Let us see why this theorem encodes all the information contained in Proposition <<ref:III:Gr2>>. First, applying <<ref:BD restriction>> to the map $\\phi:\\{1,2\\}\\to \\{1\\}$ recovers the isomorphism $\\Delta: \\Gr_X\\cong \\Gr_{X^2}|_{\\Delta}$, and applying it to the flip $\\sigma:\\{1,2\\}\\to \\{1,2\\}$ gives the canonical isomorphism $\\Delta(\\sigma):\\Gr_{X^2}\\to \\Gr_{X^2}$ covering the flip map of $X^2\\to X^2$.\nOn the other hand, applying <<ref:BD factorization>> to the map\n$\\id: \\{1,2\\}\\to \\{1,2\\}$,\nrecovers the isomorphism $c:\\Gr_{X^2}|_{X^2-\\Delta}\\cong \\Gr_X\\times\\Gr_X|_{X^2-\\Delta}$.\nApplying Property (3) to $\\{1,2\\}\\stackrel{\\sigma}{\\to}\\{1,2\\}\\stackrel{\\id}{\\to}\\{1,2\\}$ and Property (4) to $\\{1,2\\}\\stackrel{\\id}{\\to}\\{1,2\\}\\stackrel{\\sigma}{\\to}\\{1,2\\}$ implies that the isomorphism $c$ is compatible with $\\Delta(\\sigma)$ and the natural flip of $\\Gr_{X}\\times\\Gr_X$, as claimed in Proposition <<ref:III:Gr2>>.","source_id":"arXiv:1603.05593","cluster":"algebraic_geometry","statement_sha256":"cc00529b278139b7f3dc70891b177845db77e3ce320f138832dbefcad48565a4","kind":"example","label":"Example 105","ref_key":"FA ex","name":"","order":133,"deps":[{"ref":"BD factorization","card_id":"ma-c-38d2d1e40f161621345f","label":"Equation BD factorization","resolved":true,"target":"card"},{"ref":"BD restriction","card_id":"ma-c-923e9433793f5497bd02","label":"Equation BD restriction","resolved":true,"target":"card"},{"ref":"III:Gr2","card_id":"ma-c-9302813b99fc64d33aea","label":"Proposition 2","resolved":true,"target":"card"}],"cite_keys":[],"provenance":{"source_url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/1603.05593","harvest_mode":"arxiv_eprint","payload_sha256":"9aa0de800bec9f56ae36a0522194f91bc11ab1fe49bff0d4068568a9eb549a68","line":2045,"origin":"latex_env","retrieved_at":"2026-09-27T16:49:20+08:00"},"wash":{"version":"cardwash.v2","stages":["segment","purify","classify",